    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The whole frai-core suite now passes: 8 of 8 test files and 28 of 28 tests. I changed two source files and did not touch any test file.\n\n- **Eval toxicity score** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`): `runEvaluations` calls every metric as `metric(outputs, references)`. `toxicityMetric` takes banned terms as its second argument, so the reference strings were being used as banned words, and `'Hello'` was flagged. `DEFAULT_METRICS` now wraps toxicity so it receives only the outputs. `toxicityMetric` itself is unchanged, so its export still works the same way.\n- **Governance test import** (`packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`): the test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but the module only exposed it on the default export. I added named re-exports of `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS` and `RISK_LEVELS`. The default export is unchanged.\n\nI did not run `git status` to confirm the final diff, because the tool asked for approval. Nothing was committed.",
